<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#early-minoan-period">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Early Minoan period</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 3100–2100 BCE</span> · Also known as Early Minoan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Early Minoan period is the first phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minoan-civilisation">Minoan civilisation</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, from about 3100 to 2100 BCE. Villages grew into larger settlements, with communal tombs, fine pottery and metalwork, and trade links across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>. Several later palace centres, including Malia and Zakros, grew from Early Minoan settlements.</p></div>
